From: Emception maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] sysconfig: default to empty ABI flags on Windows

The native Windows interpreter used to bootstrap an Emscripten cross-build
does not expose sys.abiflags. Match the existing optional handling elsewhere
in sysconfig so the explicitly supplied target sysconfig data name can be
used without evaluating an invalid fallback.
---
 Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py b/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
--- a/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
+++ b/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
@@ -341 +341 @@
-        f'_sysconfigdata_{sys.abiflags}_{sys.platform}_{multiarch}',
+        f'_sysconfigdata_{getattr(sys, "abiflags", "")}_{sys.platform}_{multiarch}',
